==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{uder|en|fr|amphibole}}, coined by {{w|René Just Haüy}} from {{uder|en|grc|ἀμφίβολος||ambiguous}}, in reference to its many forms.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈæm.fɪˌboʊl/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|mineral}} Any of a large group of structurally similar [[hydrated]] double [[silicate]] [[minerals]], containing various combinations of [[sodium]], [[calcium]], [[magnesium]], [[iron]], and [[aluminium]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2017|author=w:Jason Isbell|title=Cumberland Gap
|passage=Remember when we could see the mountain's peak?<br>The sparkle off the '''amphibole'''.}}

